<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ken Arok</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1227</span> · Also known as Rajasa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ken Arok was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a> kingdom in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. According to Javanese chronicles he rose from humble origins to rule Tumapel, and in 1222 he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertajaya">Kertajaya</a>, the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom">Kediri</a>, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ganter">Battle of Ganter</a>. He founded the Rajasa dynasty, whose descendants later ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ken-arok.jpg" alt="Ken Arok" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eka343 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bali-lontar-Tojan-K%C3%A9nangrok.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
